<title>INDIA: Indian Seamless up 9.55 pct on bonus news.</title>
<headline>Indian Seamless up 9.55 pct on bonus news.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Indian Seamless Metal Tubes Ltd rose 4.25 rupees, or 9.55 percent to 48.75 rupees at the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The company on Monday told the BSE it would consider a bonus issue at a board meeting on February 21. Over 3,200 shares were traded at the BSE by early afternoon.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
